---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/data/site';
const updated = 'November 9, 2026';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }];
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | FalcoDash" description="How FalcoDash collects, uses and protects the information you share through falcodash.com." path="/privacy" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1 class="display-sm">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated mt-2">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section-tight">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you request an audit or contact us, we collect the details you enter: your name, email address, company, industry, phone number (if given) and message. We also record the page you submitted from, your approximate location (country, region and city) as reported by our network provider, any campaign parameters in the link you used (such as <code>utm_source</code>), the referring site, your browser's user agent and a one-way hash of your IP address, which we use to prevent spam.</p>
      <!-- REVIEW: advertising, measurement, consent and GPC language drafted 2026-11-09 for the Google Ads test. Pending Patrick's review before relying on it legally. No legal entities or addresses were added beyond what this page and the site already use. -->
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>We run our own analytics on this site. It records the pages you view, how long a page is visible, the site or campaign that referred you, your device and browser type, and your approximate location (country, region and city) derived from your IP address by our network provider. It does not use cookies. It stores a random visitor ID in your browser's local storage so repeat visits can be counted; if your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, no ID is stored. Raw IP addresses are not stored. This data stays in our own database and is not shared.</p>
      <p>This site will also use Google Analytics and Google Ads cookies for measurement and advertising. That includes measuring visits and conversions (for example, completing the AR calculator email step or booking a call) and understanding which ads led to those actions. Microsoft Clarity (which records anonymized page interactions such as clicks and scrolling) and Cloudflare Web Analytics (which uses no cookies) may also run. These services receive technical information such as the pages you view, your browser and device type and your approximate location derived from your IP address. Google Analytics, Google Ads and Clarity set cookies.</p>
      <p>We honor consent choices and the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we do not load Google Analytics, Google Ads or Clarity tags, and we do not store a first-party analytics visitor ID.</p>
      <p>You can opt out of these cookies and similar technologies by enabling Global Privacy Control in a supporting browser, by blocking cookies in your browser settings, or through Google's ad settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">adssettings.google.com</a> and the Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on. We do not sell your information.</p>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your request and schedule your audit.</li>
        <li>To send you a confirmation email for your request.</li>
        <li>To understand which pages and campaigns bring people to us.</li>
        <li>To protect the site from spam and abuse.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who processes it</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of service providers to run this site: Railway (hosting and database), Cloudflare (DNS, security and analytics), Resend (email delivery), Google (Analytics and Ads) and Microsoft (Clarity). They process data on our behalf and only as needed to provide their services.</p>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep inquiry records for as long as needed to respond and to maintain a record of our business relationship, and delete them on request.</p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete the information we hold about you by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. California residents have additional rights under the CCPA, including the right to know and the right to delete; we do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined in the CCPA.</p>
      <h2>Client data</h2>
      <p>Data we handle while building or running systems for clients is covered by our client agreements, not this policy. It stays in accounts the client owns.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>{SITE.name} · {SITE.regionName}, United States · <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> · <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
